  "problem": "In a bag containing candies, there is a $70%$ chance of getting a red candy when a random candy is taken. If $16$ candies are removed from the bag, what is the probability that fewer than $15$ candies are red? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.\n\nYou may assume that the bag contains a large number of candies and that the probability of selecting a red candy is the same on each trial.",
